# fp-fingerprint.patch - fingerprint browser patches
#
# PURPOSE: controllable fingerprint spoofing for a multi-language
# automation browser. Every behavior is driven by FP_CONFIG (JSON via
# FP_CONFIG_DATA env or FP_CONFIG file, plus FP_<KEY> env fallbacks),
# see fp_config_helpers.h (OWN FILE - never conflicts on upgrade).
# With no config, the browser behaves 100% stock (zero intervention).
#
# MERGE/UPGRADE GUIDE (new Chromium versions):
#   - Applied with patch.exe (patches/series). Any hunk mismatch aborts
#     loudly - nothing is silently skipped.
#   - After adapting hunks, regenerate with gen_patch6.py: it rewrites
#     this documentation + per-file docs from the source of truth and
#     runs a completeness check (all 54 known config keys must be
#     present in the patch) - missing keys abort generation.
#   - Risk legend per file below: LOW = stable getter anchors; MEDIUM =
#     occasionally refactored modules; HIGH = frequently changing
#     internals (WebGL/Canvas/WebRTC) - expect manual hunk adaptation.
#   - After merging, run the CDP smoke/regression suite (verifies
#     behavior, not just compilation).
# ============================================================================#

